  "notes": "Warm parchment (#f5f2eb) canvas with forest-green primary and burnt-orange CTA (Reserve, Compare). Campground thumbnails are flat vector landscape illustrations (mountains, pines, lake, orange tent) with varied sky tints rather than photos. Each result card shows a row of six small amenity icon tiles mirroring the must-have chips (amber tile when partially met) and amber warning lines from reviews ('Mosquitoes in late May'). Detail header shows must-haves as check chips plus quoted review-mention chips with counts. The site map is a hand-drawn-style SVG plan: loops as rounded ovals, tree blobs for shade, WC markers, hatched 'Generators allowed' zone, reservoir at the bottom, scale bar; site dots coloured by availability with a dark callout for the selected site. Site list rows show restroom distance as a mini bar plus Sat/Sun/Mon night chips. Sticky dark compare tray at the bottom of the results list opens a modal comparison table (saved campgrounds as columns, BEST badges, 'Copy summary to share'). Glossary terms are dotted-underlined and open dark definition bubbles; must-have chips carry title tooltips explaining what they hide."
